---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/pages/about.css';
import Citation from '../components/Citation.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Laurie Di Francesco · visual artist working through photography and writing."
  image="/images/og-home.jpg"
>

  <!-- ── Titre + Épigraphe ────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="about-head container">
    <p class="about-eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="about-h1">Laurie Di Francesco</h1>

    <Citation author="Aristotle · Metaphysics, Book A">
      All men by nature desire to know. An indication of this is the delight we
      take in our senses; for even apart from their usefulness they are loved for
      themselves; and above all others the sense of sight.
    </Citation>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Bio ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <div class="about-bio">

    <div class="bio-marg">

      <!-- Origins -->
      <div class="bio-marg-lab">Origins</div>
      <div class="bio-marg-par">
        <p>Laurie Di Francesco is a photographer and author, largely self-taught.</p>
        <p>She grew up between France and Italy, then discovered Brazil, which became a third home.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Approach -->
      <div class="bio-marg-lab">Approach</div>
      <div class="bio-marg-par">
        <p>She gives image to intimate narratives about displacement, geographical first, inner afterwards. Her projects trace the movements that precede a transformation, and return again and again to the notion of the threshold, as the invitation of a line to be crossed.</p>
        <p>Her language is poetic, sensory and philosophical. She thinks and speaks in several languages, whose rhythms she works with.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Work -->
      <div class="bio-marg-lab">Work</div>
      <div class="bio-marg-par">
        <p>She is currently working on two series. <em>Quando sono qui, non sono là</em> questions the possibility of a rebirth after a childhood held back. <em>La Mer en Corps</em> documents the relation of a weakened body to the sea, weaving together physical effort, new technologies and film photography.</p>
        <p>Her first exhibition was held in Brazil, in Belo Horizonte, in 2024, and she joined the French collective Monolit in 2026.</p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- ── Refs table ──────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="bio-refs">
      <div>
        <p class="bio-refs-title">Collective</p>
        <p class="bio-refs-content">Monolit<br />founded by Orianne Ciantar Olive</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="bio-refs-title">Training</p>
        <p class="bio-refs-content">Ateliê da Imagem, Rio de Janeiro<br />ENSP, Arles<br />Les Rencontres de la Photographie d'Arles</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="bio-refs-title">Workshops</p>
        <p class="bio-refs-content">Fabienne Pavia, Éditions Le Bec en l'Air<br />Antoine d'Agata<br />Klavdij Sluban</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bio-refs-block--large">
        <p class="bio-refs-title">Inspirations</p>
        <p class="bio-refs-content bio-refs-content--justif">Claudia Andujar&nbsp;· Graciela Iturbide&nbsp;· Luigi Ghirri&nbsp;· Letizia Battaglia&nbsp;· Jacques-Henri Lartigue&nbsp;· Manuel Álvarez Bravo&nbsp;· Miguel Rio Branco&nbsp;· José Diniz&nbsp;· Franco Zecchin&nbsp;· Clube da Esquina&nbsp;· Sufjan Stevens&nbsp;· Clarice Lispector&nbsp;· Paolo Sorrentino&nbsp;· Henri Matisse</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Sortie ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="bio-outro">
      <span class="bio-outro-label">Next</span>
      <a class="bio-outro-link" href="/work">See the work →</a>
    </div>

  </div>

</Layout>
